    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74002.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "I remember the back and forth between Ronald Reagan and Sam Donaldson. And Sam Donaldson and Ronald Reagan ended up liking each other. And Reagan always took his ridiculous attacks and questions and it was a back and forth and Reagan did a lot of this. And people were complaining that Reagan was too old. And if I recall Ted, I'm pretty sure I'm right about this. When he was running for president, the media was saying, are you getting too old today's your birthday? And you're gonna be 69. And he said, no, it's just the 30th anniversary of my 39th birthday. But they literally were trying to pretend like he was too old at 69 years old. This guy's going to be 85 if he runs and wins again by the time he's out of office. And we've already seen the cognitive decline. If you look at Joe Biden 10 years ago, we even said he's a way different person than he is today. So why are they still hanging their hat on him? And do you think like a Gavin Newsom is in the wings?",
