    "turn_text": "Well, our policy now is it is not an independent entity. And it is part of China. That is the official U.S. policy. But it has always been our policy that we would defend Taiwan if attacks, especially by mainland China. I'm not so sure that that's our policy anymore. I think down the road China is going to walk in to Taiwan. The Taiwanese might be able to defend themselves to some extent. But I think the U.S. and its commitment years ago to defend Taiwan won't occur, we'll be missing in action when that occurs. China is making all of the moves to just walk in to Taiwan and we will not, I don't think we'll do a thing about it.",
