    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74002.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 59,
    "turn_text": "That is exactly what it is. The piecemeal is across the board in every activity by the left. And this is just one more example of that, preventing a person's free exercise of speech. We're not talking about actions, we're talking about the free exercises speech. And just remember, the rule is you're not, you don't commit a crime if you are offended by what somebody says, you don't have the right to say, he committed a crime against me because he hurt my feelings. Well, I'm sorry, that's not the law. Accountability goes to the person who is making the statement or doing the action and it's the action of the individual that should be criminalized not the person who says something happened to me, I'm offended. Therefore, this person committed a crime. They have to have the",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
